      "claim": "L3 dihydroergocryptine/dihydroergocristine records show very low plasma exposure after oral dosing (Cmax 96.6–263.3 pg/mL; AUCinf 387.8–1220.4 pg·h/mL after 10–20 mg), and erythromycin coadministration raises DHEC Cmax ~9.5-fold, indicating extensive CYP3A4-mediated first-pass metabolism in this class.",
      "card_ids": ["C57","C48","C55","C88","C80","C91","C59","C68","C81"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "DHE oral AUC ratios (~37–45% of IV) are less transferable because DHE differs in side-chain composition and dihydro saturation; they do not establish F≥20% for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C54","C72","C46","C83","C75","C84"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Low-F records for sofosbuvir and saquinavir are directionally consistent but have low structural transfer to the ergot-peptide query; they are not the primary basis for the low prediction.",
      "card_ids": ["C26","C28","C38","C39"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "L4 solubility/permeability records for unrelated scaffolds (fexofenadine, tadalafil, nintedanib, danoprevir, vinblastine, etc.) do not provide affirmative threshold-relevant evidence for the query.",
      "card_ids": ["C95","C100","C105","C118","C130","C143","C144"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
      "family": "intestinal_absorption_permeability",
      "applicability": "low",
      "direction": "neutral_or_unclear",
      "decision_effect": "no_change",
      "card_ids": ["C95","C100","C105","C118","C130","C143","C144"]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct absolute oral bioavailability measurement for the query molecule (bromocriptine) in the supplied records.",
    "No query-specific intestinal permeability or solubility data in L4; closest L4 records are for unrelated scaffolds.",
    "L3 ergot analogs are dihydro derivatives lacking the query's bromine and 9,10-unsaturation; DHE differs in side-chain composition.",
    "No formulation, dose, or human PK data for the query are supplied."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L4 provides no query-relevant intestinal absorption/permeability/solubility evidence; the low prediction is retained on the basis of structurally relevant L3 ergot-peptide low-exposure and first-pass records, with moderate confidence."
